## Message table (party game data; relay adds `from`)

| t | sender → | fields | meaning |
|---|---|---|---|
| `maze` | each seat → all | `json` (double-serialised MazeData), `by` | own maze (same shape as 1v1) |
| `ready_for_maze` | seat → `to` holder | — | re-request a missing maze; the holder replies with its `maze` payload `to` the requester |
| `arena_ready` | each → all | — | built and spawned |
| `go` | host → all | — | start the 3-2-1 (host sends once every roster seat is arena_ready) |
| `loadout` | host → all | `start` (int), `arena` (int[] of length n−1, distinct) | guns |
| `pos` / `shot` / `reload` / `dryfire` / `gunsel` | each → all | exactly as 1v1 | cosmetic + movement |
| `gate_down` | each → all | `id` | as 1v1 (builder names `Maze{seat}`) |
| `zone` | each → all | `m` (maze seat or −1) | which maze/hall the sender is in (`MazeAt`) |
| `hit` | shooter → `to` victim | `dmg`, `px,py,pz` | as 1v1, but directed |
| `dmg` | victim → all | `by`, `amt` | validated damage taken (feeds the shared table) |
| `die` | victim → all | `by` (killer seat, −1 if none) | local death |
| `pickup_claim` | seat → host (`to`) | `i` | claim pickup i |
| `pickup_awarded` | host → all | `i`, `seat` | the verdict (host applies its own immediately) |

Leavers arrive as the NetworkManager `PeerLeft(seat, hostSeat)` signal. Also replay `_nm.PendingPeerLefts` at `_Ready` (the Phase 4 pattern).

